// THE BYPASS THE PER-STORE SEALS DO NOT CLOSE, RECORDED AS AN EXPECTING-RED HOLE (DESIGN section 4b(4)). The
// attempt_lifecycle operations take a plain SlotStore, and gunbc.durable_cas_file_store file_slot_store_over is
// public and path-taking, so a module outside every store's file can open an attempt over a literal path and
// nothing refuses it: this asserts the census carries NO blocking diagnostic beyond the baseline. The seals above
// protect only the business functions that take a sealed record. The day the wall lands (ambient filesystem
// authority removed: the filesystem arrives as an entry-point argument and local_filesystem stops being a global)
// this goes red and is rewritten to expect the refusal, becoming the permanent regression control. Residual row:
// gunbc.durable_cas_file_store slot_store_legacy_root_dissolution, owned by #14944.
test fn a_foreign_attempt_open_over_a_literal_path_is_still_accepted() -> ProcessExit {
  census_exit(blocking_delta(hostile: plain_store_attempt_open_source, safe: closure_baseline_source, holds: fn(n) { n <= 0 }))
}
